sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: To set up a straight line at right angles to a given plane from a given point in it.
----
proof:

Let the plane of reference be the given plane and {A} the point in it.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="240" height="200" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="XI.12 diagram" src="propXI12.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // Joyce's figure: the plane of reference P drawn in oblique view, with A
    // in it, BC dropped from the elevated point B, and AD parallel to BC
    // (D = A + B − C).
    //
    // Added: PT, a transparent faceless twin of P (the filled plane would
    // be raised over the figure if highlighted, #140). BC and AD are
    // declared from B and from A, so they stroke as drawn without twins.
    // The text names no angle (only lines at right angles to the plane),
    // so there are no angle markers.
    //
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): X, Y, Z (far-off direction
    // points), P0, A free; P1, P3 sliders; B free and C a slider. B and C
    // arrive with "From an elevated point B draw BC", so they are deferred.
    // D and P2 are derived and listed per slide.
    var GIVEN = ["P","PT","P2","A"];
    var BCv   = GIVEN.concat(["B","C","BC"]);
    var ALL   = BCv.concat(["D","AD"]);
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "XI.12",
        elements: [
            "X;point;free;100000,100",
            "Y;point;free;100,-100000",
            "Z;point;free;50000,-100000",
            "P0;point;free;30,170;0;0,75,100",
            "P1;point;lineSlider;P0,X,160,170;0;30,75,100",
            "P3;point;lineSlider;P0,Z,90,90;0;30,75,100",
            "P2;point;parallelogram;P3,P0,P1;0;0",
            "P;polygon;quadrilateral;P0,P1,P2,P3;0;0;lightGray;brighter",
            "A;point;free;80,140",
            "B;point;free;150,40",
            "C;point;lineSlider;B,Y,150,120",
            "BC;line;connect;B,C",
            "D;point;parallelogram;A,C,B",
            "AD;line;connect;A,D",
            // Transparent highlight target.
            "PT;polygon;quadrilateral;P0,P1,P2,P3;0;0;0;0"
        ],
        deferDraggables: ["B","C"],
        slides: [
            { text: "“To set up a straight line at right angles to a given plane from a given point in it.”",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["A","PT"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "XI.12" }] },
            { text: "Let the {plane of reference|PT} be the given plane and {A} the point in it.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["PT","A"] },
            { text: "It is required to set up from the point {A} a straight line at right angles to the {plane of reference|PT}.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["A","PT"] },
            { text: "From an elevated point {B} draw {BC} perpendicular to the {plane of reference|PT},",
              visible: BCv,
              highlighted: ["BC","PT"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "B",  name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "BC", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "C",  name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "BC perpendicular to the plane", ref: "XI.11" }] },
            { text: "and draw {AD} parallel to {BC} through the point {A}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AD","BC"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "AD", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "D",  name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "AD parallel to BC", ref: "I.31" }] },
            { text: "Then since {AD} and {BC} are two parallel straight lines,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AD","BC"] },
            { text: "and one of them, {BC}, is at right angles to the {plane of reference|PT},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["BC","PT"] },
            { text: "therefore the remaining one, {AD}, is also at right angles to the {plane of reference|PT}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AD","PT"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "parallel to a line at right angles to a plane", ref: "XI.8" }] },
            { text: "Therefore {AD} is set up at right angles to the given plane from the point {A} in it.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AD","A","PT"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.F." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "XI.12") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "I.31":  "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI31/",
        "XI.8":  "/elements/books/bookXI/propositions/propXI8/",
        "XI.11": "/elements/books/bookXI/propositions/propXI11/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

It is required to set up from the point {A} a straight line at right angles to the plane of reference.

From an elevated point {B} draw {BC} perpendicular to the plane of reference, and draw {AD} parallel to {BC} through the point {A}. [!just XI.11, I.31]

Then since {AD} and {BC} are two parallel straight lines, and one of them, {BC}, is at right angles to the plane of reference, therefore the remaining one, {AD}, is also at right angles to the plane of reference. [!just XI.8]

Therefore {AD} is set up at right angles to the given plane from the point {A} in it.

<div class="qed">Q.E.F.</div>
<br clear="all">
----
guide: This proposition, like the last, is used frequently in the rest of the *Elements* to construct lines perpendicular to planes.
